# index column sets don't change, only the names. On PostgreSQL we rename
# whichever variant exists, with no-ops for the rest:
#
#   - 'zinnia_entr_*_pubdate_idx': fresh deploys that ran 0003_publication_date
#     against the smartlgt fork, where the indexes were created with
#     explicit name= arguments.
#   - 'zinnia_entry_*_<hash>_idx': legacy deploys whose 0001/0003 were
#     faked or ran against an upstream zinnia that had Meta.indexes
#     without name=, so Django auto-named them.
#
# On other backends (SQLite test DBs, etc.) the DB-side rename is skipped
# entirely — query plans don't care about index names, only column sets,
# and SQLite has no ALTER INDEX ... RENAME TO syntax. The state_operations
# keep Django's autodetector quiet on every backend.

